  "case": "cf3_temperature",
  "question": "How should temperature and residence time be coordinated in Route 3 at 70 °C versus 80 °C? Compare apparent activation energies, orders, processed observations and predictions.",
  "scientific_facts": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "text": "At the same feed composition, catalyst concentration and 1717.09 s, predicted yield/selectivity is 73.96%/89.35% at 70 °C and 74.27%/85.24% at 80 °C. Yield and selectivity must be compared separately.",
      "role": "comparison",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "kinetics:tbhp_cf3",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-70",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-80"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "text": "Main reaction: apparent Ea = 123.435 kJ/mol, ln A = 31.4283, orders catalyst 1.496, H₂O₂ 2.306, TBA 0.749; Side reaction: apparent Ea = 118.799 kJ/mol, ln A = 31.5161, orders catalyst 1.517, TBA 0.050, TBHP 0.079. These parameters describe the calibrated system and do not establish an elementary mechanism.",
      "role": "parameters",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "kinetics:tbhp_cf3",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-70",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-80"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "text": "At fixed instantaneous concentrations, heating from the lower to the higher temperature multiplies the main rate by 3.405 and the side rate by 3.252. These are rate multipliers, not final-yield multipliers.",
      "role": "explanation",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "kinetics:tbhp_cf3",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-70",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-80"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "text": "The concentration factor in the side/main rate ratio is catalyst^0.021 × TBA^-0.699 × TBHP^0.079 × H2O2^-2.306. Competition changes as feedstocks are consumed and TBHP accumulates. The integrated side-reaction consumption of TBHP is 0.3315 and 0.4838 mol/L at the lower and higher temperatures, respectively.",
      "role": "explanation",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "kinetics:tbhp_cf3",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-70",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-80"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "text": "For this endpoint, 70 °C gives higher predicted selectivity. Temperature and residence time should be screened together. At the higher temperature, the predicted TBHP maximum is at approximately 635.3 s on a 8.6-s grid; longer residence does not necessarily increase target yield.",
      "role": "decision",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "kinetics:tbhp_cf3",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-70",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-80"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "text": "Across 200 converged parameter-bootstrap draws, the conditional 95% interval for lower-minus-higher-temperature yield is [-1.92, 1.09] percentage points. The interval includes zero, so the yield ordering is unresolved under this conditional uncertainty. Model-form and data-processing uncertainty are not included.",
      "role": "uncertainty",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "kinetics:tbhp_cf3",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-70",
        "experiment:tbhp_cf3:1.9-1.25-80"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F7",
      "text": "For paired processed experimental observations, the higher-minus-lower-temperature yield difference is 6.37 percentage points, versus 0.31 percentage points predicted. These observations participated in fitting; this is a residual check, not held-out validation. The discrepancy requires checking the condition-specific time series; parameter intervals do not represent model discrepancy.",
